  "_about": "Components: the equipment a mech's die is made of. Each is exactly one entry on the die (its face: the engine's word for one entry). Nothing generic exists: every entry on a die is a component, or an empty hardpoint. A component a chassis lists under fixed is built in and is never bought or crafted, which is what makes it unique. Numbers are in tens. Kinetic entries carry power and power_max and roll between them, and may crit; energy entries are static and never crit. Keywords are a list; authored entries should stay under the validator's cap, upgrades may push past it. passive is null or one object, same shape as a chassis passive. Shown to the player: codex (the inspect entry), flavour (a quote); both still to be written. design is internal and never shown: fantasy, niche. Numbers are placeholders.",
